    <content type="html"><![CDATA[
<div class="bloglink" href="https://xixs.com/blog/micro-2026/2026-10-20-215224.html" style="cursor: pointer;" onclick="window.location.href=this.getAttribute('href')">
 <div class="bloglink-date">2026-10-20<div class="bloglink-time">21:52:24</div></div>
 <div class="blogbody"><p>Ecstatica is an interesting one, yeah its old but it shows how a custom 
renderer can produce an art style that still works even though 
technology advances.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gl4GpXFDh3s">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gl4GpXFDh3s</a></p>
<p>I mean, I would say we have enough oomph to do real time metaballs now 
and y&#39;know, you could upgrade the characters into the metaballs they 
always wanted to be.</p>
<p>Maybe even sdfs and a marching renderer and you get shadows+reflections 
for almost free.</p>
<p>Or maybe that would break it, anyway it is a style that still 
works today.</p>
<p>Oh yeah and the game is nice and weird survival horror &quot;Alone in the 
Dark&quot; adventure sort of thing.</p>
<p>Demo now on steam...</p>
<p><a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4834840/Ecstatica/">https://store.steampowered.com/app/4834840/Ecstatica/</a>
<br/>
<br/></p>
</div>
</div>
]]></content>
